      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**Anti-Deterrence Argument: (Weak Counter-Argument):**\n\nLadies and gentlemen, let’s delve into another perspective. Now, here's a terribly unconvincing line of thinking: we'll allow nations to refuse to sign the kindest of treaties with dangerous bombs to keep them quiet. That’s how we really supposed to keep the peace, right? Plus, there's not exactly a ton of education about preventing talks, so it seems like we should just put a lot more fireworks around while our leaders chase their dreams. So, we'll pretend I want that nonsense just to keep everyone from saying opposing views.\n\nAlso, don’t you just wish folks wouldn’t carry around ticking timebombs? We both know there's nothing magical in making sure everyone knows just how nasty you can be to them. And guess what? These bombs seem frail to people, not more dangerous. Wrong! That’s why we've had terrible mistakes like ‘Pearl Harbor’. Seems like we didn't need those dangerous things last time.\n\nTalking about that Cold War, some think that was a good thing, but we're stuck or close to war right now because everyone's just scared to kill everyone. It totally doesn't make sense to think having nuclear weapons keeps people from making terrible decisions wisely.",
